    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d575-a3">

                <pb facs="0959" n="889" sameAs="frus:frus1883/pg889"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 3 in No. 298.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Lord Dufferin to Mr.
                            Heap.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Therapia</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1883-11-07"><hi rendition="#italic">November</hi> 7,
                        1883</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to the dispatch I addressed
                    to you on the 5th instant, in which I informed you that Mr. Knapp had identified
                    Moussa Bey as one of his assailants in the attack made upon him in May last, I
                    have the honor to transmit to you herewith, <pb facs="0960" n="890"
                        xml:id="pg890"/> for your information, a dispatch, which I have just
                    received from Her Majesty’s consul at Erzroom on this subject.</p>
                <p>You will perceive from Colonel Everett’s dispatch that it is considered that
                    unless strong pressure is brought to bear upon the Sublime Porte there is very
                    little chance &amp;hat Moussa Bey will ever be brought to justice.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>DUFFERIN.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
